1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,840
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:03,340
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:07,210 --> 00:00:08,650
(Episode 43)

4
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:52,660
Ms. Jo.

5
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:58,660
Dr. Ju.

6
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:03,300
What do I do?

7
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:08,040
What am I going to do, Dr. Ju?

8
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:09,840
It is all right.

9
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,280
It is all right.

10
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:24,320
Please don't say anything...

11
00:01:25,990 --> 00:01:27,760
to my family.

12
00:01:29,390 --> 00:01:32,460
You must tell your family soon.

13
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:35,100
That's the very first thing
you need to do.

14
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:37,870
I will.

15
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:40,510
I'll tell them myself.

16
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:44,540
This isn't something
you can handle on your own.

17
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:47,710
It's not that I'm trying
to handle it alone...

18
00:01:49,210 --> 00:01:51,450
Right now, I honestly
don't even know...

19
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,280
what to say to them first.

20
00:01:57,290 --> 00:01:59,220
Please just treat me
like nothing happened.

21
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:01,290
Just act normal.

22
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:05,230
Don't look shocked
when you see me...

23
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:08,870
and don't let my family
notice anything.

24
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:12,670
I'm begging you.

25
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:17,210
All right.

26
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,280
I won't tell them before you do.

27
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:23,750
Still, please don't wait too long.

28
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:35,960
Should I just send it like this?

29
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:39,060
Could you give me
the patient ID number?

30
00:02:40,370 --> 00:02:41,370
Yes, that's right.

31
00:02:41,930 --> 00:02:44,970
Jo Mi Mi. That's an unusual name.

32
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:46,470
(Jo Mi Mi, Cancer Center,
Attending Dr. Yoo Tae Gyeong)

33
00:02:48,910 --> 00:02:51,180
I can never get used to this,
no matter how many times I do it.

34
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:53,410
Why?

35
00:02:54,550 --> 00:02:56,210
I have to send an appointment
confirmation text,

36
00:02:56,810 --> 00:02:57,820
but she's a cancer patient.

37
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:12,900
We cleaned up the silhouette...

38
00:03:13,060 --> 00:03:14,130
so they won't look awkward
with skirts.

39
00:03:14,370 --> 00:03:16,200
They're comfortable enough
for daily commutes, too.

40
00:03:16,670 --> 00:03:18,540
We've also kept the price
accessible, CEO Jeon.

41
00:03:18,970 --> 00:03:20,910
Here is the projected retail price.

42
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:26,210
There's nothing
distinctive about it.

43
00:03:26,950 --> 00:03:30,450
- Except for the low price.
- Then what else...

44
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,650
should we improve?

45
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:36,050
Customers need a clear reason
why they must buy this right now.

46
00:03:36,390 --> 00:03:38,690
There are plenty of similar options.
Why choose this?

47
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:43,160
The only draw is its low price
as a promotional item.

48
00:03:43,230 --> 00:03:45,430
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

49
00:03:50,570 --> 00:03:52,500
Have Head Designer Cha
from Design come in.

50
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:53,770
Yes, CEO Jeon.

51
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:58,310
Yes, understood. I'll go right up.

52
00:03:59,080 --> 00:04:00,080
Right.

53
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:05,950
Kang Da Mi.
Where on earth have you been again?

54
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,020
I had a phone call
that I really had to take.

55
00:04:09,320 --> 00:04:10,820
I'm sorry.
I'll get back to work now.

56
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:12,390
Follow me.

57
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:14,730
Pardon? Where to?

58
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:20,370
- Let's go, Head Designer Cha.
- Right.

59
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:34,280
I believe I only asked for you,
Head Designer Cha.

60
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,810
I thought having
my assistant listen in...

61
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:37,220
would help things move faster.

62
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:40,550
Step inside.

63
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,830
These sneakers are designed
to be worn with skirts.

64
00:04:48,290 --> 00:04:50,860
Product Planning
developed them exclusively,

65
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,130
but there's nothing distinctive
besides the price.

66
00:04:54,930 --> 00:04:58,400
I wanted to get your input,
so I asked you to come up.

67
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:02,870
Do you have any good ideas,
Head Designer Cha?

68
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,210
May I try them on?

69
00:05:09,810 --> 00:05:10,850
You, Kang Da Mi?

70
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,580
Yes, I would like to try them on.

71
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,940
Mom, wait, stop.

72
00:05:38,810 --> 00:05:40,480
Your shoelace is untied again.

73
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,950
Oh, so it is.

74
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,680
No, no.

75
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:49,450
I showed you how to tie it
so it will not come loose.

76
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:53,190
Just pull it tight once like this
and tie it.

77
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:55,130
You showed me,
but I keep forgetting.

78
00:05:55,860 --> 00:05:58,260
Wait until you get to my age,
sweetie.

79
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:00,360
The moment you turn around,
you forget.

80
00:06:03,070 --> 00:06:05,200
Really?
Then I guess I have no choice.

81
00:06:05,670 --> 00:06:08,070
I will tie your shoelaces for you
for the rest of your life.

82
00:06:08,970 --> 00:06:09,970
Really?

83
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:11,580
That is a promise.

84
00:06:12,510 --> 00:06:16,180
Okay. I am being very generous, Mom.

85
00:06:16,550 --> 00:06:20,220
I am living the good life
thanks to my wonderful daughter.

86
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,790
Thank you, my dear daughter.

87
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:24,260
Do not mention it.

88
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:27,020
Go on, ma'am.

89
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:30,930
Now that I moved out,
I cannot even do that for her.

90
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:33,200
Kang Da Mi.

91
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,200
Yes? Right.

92
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:50,880
About those shoelaces,

93
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:53,680
is there something we can do?

94
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:58,720
When women are busy working,
having laces come untied...

95
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,990
can be pretty inconvenient, right?

96
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:04,460
What about hook-and-loop?
I mean, Velcro.

97
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:06,360
Velcro?

98
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:12,270
My mom's laces kept coming undone,
so I used to tie them for her often.

99
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:14,110
If we use Velcro,

100
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:16,940
there are no laces to come undone,
and there is no need to tie them.

101
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:21,180
A sleek, laceless design
would go well with suits,

102
00:07:21,210 --> 00:07:24,020
and I think they would look
even better with skirts.

103
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:27,750
That is not a bad idea.

104
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:30,960
CEO Jeon, if we switch to Velcro,

105
00:07:31,090 --> 00:07:32,790
it will inevitably drive up
the retail price.

106
00:07:33,220 --> 00:07:34,460
I do not think it is feasible.

107
00:07:34,790 --> 00:07:37,730
Well, can't you find other ways
to bring down the unit cost?

108
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:40,970
After all, that is your job,
Assistant Manager Kang.

109
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:47,510
Incorporate the Velcro idea,
make a new sample, and report back.

110
00:07:48,470 --> 00:07:49,470
Yes, CEO Jeon.

111
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,440
Maybe it's
your extensive retail experience.

112
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:56,110
You come up with
great practical ideas.

113
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,650
Not at all.

114
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:00,590
It just crossed my mind.

115
00:08:01,920 --> 00:08:04,420
It really is a great idea,
Kang Da Mi.

116
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:08,030
Head Designer Cha,
please support Product Planning.

117
00:08:08,290 --> 00:08:11,060
You too, Kang Da Mi.
We are pressed for time.

118
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:12,660
Yes, understood.

119
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:24,080
(Product Planning Department)

120
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:25,610
- Let us talk inside.
- Yes.

121
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:30,280
Hey.

122
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:31,880
Yes, Assistant Manager Kang?

123
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:33,990
There is no reason
to be so thrilled.

124
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,090
Just because you had one good idea,

125
00:08:37,190 --> 00:08:38,490
do not get ahead of yourself.

126
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:42,790
You might think CEO Jeon
has finally acknowledged you,

127
00:08:43,230 --> 00:08:46,230
but CEO Jeon
is not that easy to impress.

128
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,070
It's true that I'm happy,

129
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:50,840
but I'm not reading more into it.

130
00:08:51,900 --> 00:08:54,570
I will keep your advice in mind.
Thank you, Assistant Manager Kang.

131
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,740
But Assistant Manager Kang...

132
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:01,210
- What?
- Like I told you before,

133
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:04,980
my name is Kang Da Mi, not "hey."

134
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:08,290
From now on, I would appreciate it
if you used my name.

135
00:09:09,050 --> 00:09:10,190
Please.

136
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:20,030
She should be trying to please me.
What is her problem?

137
00:09:29,510 --> 00:09:30,640
You scared me.

138
00:09:31,510 --> 00:09:32,580
What is that, anyway?

139
00:09:33,010 --> 00:09:34,580
This? Abalone.

140
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:39,550
It has been so long
since I had abalone. Nice.

141
00:09:39,780 --> 00:09:41,120
Oh, it is not for you.

142
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:43,150
I bought it for my mom.

143
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,490
Well, good for you.

144
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:48,460
If you make plenty,
we can have some, too.

145
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:49,890
There is only one.

146
00:09:50,430 --> 00:09:52,200
It was expensive.

147
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:56,800
Whatever. It is not like
we cannot have it later.

148
00:09:57,840 --> 00:10:01,040
Let us make it for Mother first
and get back in her good graces.

149
00:10:01,810 --> 00:10:04,010
You know making porridge
is my specialty. Give it here.

150
00:10:04,080 --> 00:10:05,080
All right.

151
00:10:09,410 --> 00:10:10,410
All right.

152
00:10:14,790 --> 00:10:17,760
(No Parking)

153
00:10:18,890 --> 00:10:22,860
(Swissoland Unmanned Motel)

154
00:10:22,930 --> 00:10:26,030
(Motel)

155
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:34,010
(Entrance)

156
00:10:34,040 --> 00:10:35,570
(Self-Check-In)

157
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:38,980
They said he was definitely here.
Why is he not coming out?

158
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:42,280
How much longer, darn it?

159
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:57,090
(119 Paramedics)

160
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,040
No way.

161
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,190
Kim Pro.

162
00:11:30,590 --> 00:11:33,860
Identity confirmed.
Name is Kim Dong Seok.

163
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,470
ID number starts with 870102.

164
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:42,870
Hey.

165
00:11:43,670 --> 00:11:44,840
Kim Dong Seok, you...

166
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:02,090
The customer you are calling
is unavailable.

167
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,330
Please leave a message
after the tone.

168
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:13,300
Sir. Where are you, really?

169
00:12:14,210 --> 00:12:15,470
What do I do now?

170
00:12:16,310 --> 00:12:18,140
What? What do you mean?

171
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:20,140
It is all over now.

172
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,880
What is over, sir?

173
00:12:29,990 --> 00:12:31,090
Do not tell me...

174
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,220
You are not at the Han River,
are you?

175
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,160
Where are you?

176
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:38,630
I will come to you, sir.

177
00:12:38,930 --> 00:12:40,500
Just tell me
where you are right now.

178
00:12:41,700 --> 00:12:43,800
You must not do anything reckless,
you know that, right?

179
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:45,270
Why would you come?

180
00:12:46,670 --> 00:12:49,410
- I'll come to you.
- Wait. Don't hang up.

181
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:01,890
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

182
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:11,160
Mother, give us a real smile
this time.

183
00:13:11,230 --> 00:13:12,600
- Right.
- Ye Ri, get closer to Grandma.

184
00:13:12,660 --> 00:13:15,230
- Okay, okay.
- We just took one earlier.

185
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:16,930
Why take another?

186
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,440
I am taking this one
with my phone, Mother.

187
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,840
All right, smile naturally.

188
00:13:21,910 --> 00:13:24,040
- One, two, three.
- Good.

189
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:26,810
It turned out great, right?

190
00:13:26,880 --> 00:13:29,010
Yes, yes. Honey,
come get in the picture too.

191
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:30,080
- Me too?
- Come over here.

192
00:13:30,150 --> 00:13:31,180
All right, all right. I'm coming.

193
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:36,150
- Now.
- Mom, this way now.

194
00:13:36,390 --> 00:13:37,860
Look here. Ready?

195
00:13:38,420 --> 00:13:39,690
Smile.

196
00:13:40,420 --> 00:13:43,330
Everyone, smile. One, two, three.

197
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,160
One, two, three.

198
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:48,970
- Smile, everyone.
- Smile.

199
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:51,370
One, two, three.

200
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,380
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

201
00:14:00,510 --> 00:14:01,510
I am back.

202
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:03,880
Mi Mi.

203
00:14:04,880 --> 00:14:08,090
Mi Mi.
Where have you been all this time?

204
00:14:09,050 --> 00:14:10,920
I just stopped by to show my face.

205
00:14:11,990 --> 00:14:16,030
I am tired, so I am going to rest.
Mother, I am heading in first.

206
00:14:22,730 --> 00:14:23,730
Unbelievable.

207
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:27,940
She went out for fun, stayed out
all night, and now wants to rest?

208
00:14:28,710 --> 00:14:31,910
I tried to bite my tongue,
but this is ridiculous.

209
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:33,040
Ri Ja.

210
00:14:34,950 --> 00:14:36,650
Make sure you do your work
properly without me.

211
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,890
What is she talking about?

212
00:14:44,460 --> 00:14:46,890
Excuse me, Mrs. Choi.

213
00:14:47,560 --> 00:14:49,430
What is wrong with my sister?

214
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:51,930
How can she have the nerve
to act like that?

215
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:57,570
- She is acting strange, isn't she?
- Yes, very strange.

216
00:14:57,840 --> 00:15:00,070
Mrs. Choi, why don't you go in
and say something to her?

217
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:04,040
- Snap her back to her senses.
- She won't even look me...

218
00:15:04,170 --> 00:15:05,340
in the eye anymore.

219
00:15:05,980 --> 00:15:07,080
Let us just leave her be.

220
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:11,420
Unbelievable.

221
00:15:48,050 --> 00:15:49,150
Why should I settle for this?

222
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:52,560
If I am having some,
I should have something good.

223
00:15:54,060 --> 00:15:56,760
I received some as a gift before.
It must be put away somewhere.

224
00:16:30,260 --> 00:16:32,060
("Don't Be Surprised!" Plays)

225
00:16:45,510 --> 00:16:46,510
Mom.

226
00:16:47,410 --> 00:16:48,410
What?

227
00:16:50,410 --> 00:16:52,320
What are you reading?

228
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,090
I mean...

229
00:16:55,650 --> 00:16:57,790
You stayed out all night
and aren't even at the restaurant.

230
00:16:58,190 --> 00:16:59,190
Aren't you going to close up?

231
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:01,430
And brewed coffee?

232
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:03,690
Am I not allowed
to drink brewed coffee?

233
00:17:04,630 --> 00:17:06,760
Is there a rule that says
I can only drink instant coffee?

234
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:08,700
It is not that.

235
00:17:09,330 --> 00:17:11,870
It is just unusual.
It just seems so unlike you.

236
00:17:13,870 --> 00:17:15,010
Don't bother me.

237
00:17:15,670 --> 00:17:16,670
I'm tired of everything.

238
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:22,210
If you are so worried
about the restaurant,

239
00:17:22,210 --> 00:17:23,550
go out there and help.

240
00:17:23,910 --> 00:17:25,550
All right.

241
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:29,050
Grandma, what are you reading?

242
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,920
A book of plays.

243
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:36,230
Everything people say
is written right here, Su Ah.

244
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:41,870
You mean what people say on stage?
I went to see one with Mom before.

245
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:44,230
Did you?

246
00:17:44,670 --> 00:17:47,100
That is right.
Because of these scripts,

247
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:49,640
the actors can perform up on stage.

248
00:17:55,610 --> 00:17:57,980
It is weird.

249
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:00,920
Mom is acting so weird.

250
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:05,060
It is weird, so weird. Really weird.

251
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:06,660
Weird.

252
00:18:06,990 --> 00:18:07,990
Fascinating, isn't it?

253
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:11,760
Now, turn the page, and it begins.

254
00:18:13,860 --> 00:18:16,330
Auntie.

255
00:18:16,730 --> 00:18:17,870
Guess what I just saw?

256
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:21,770
- What? What is it now?
- Mom is...

257
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:27,340
drinking coffee and reading a book.
She even had music playing.

258
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,150
She was in that yellow dress, too.

259
00:18:29,810 --> 00:18:30,810
Your mother?

260
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:34,890
Yes. I brought up the restaurant,

261
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:36,750
and she told me
to go help out instead.

262
00:18:38,290 --> 00:18:41,120
See? Something is definitely off.

263
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:42,930
What is with her?

264
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:45,260
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

265
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:46,660
So weird.

266
00:18:48,570 --> 00:18:51,600
This one is wide,
so it will cover more of the instep.

267
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:54,070
Sort them into two groups first...

268
00:18:54,370 --> 00:18:56,340
so we can check both the shape
and the fit.

269
00:18:57,040 --> 00:18:58,040
Yes, Head Designer Cha.

270
00:19:03,850 --> 00:19:06,280
Thank you, everyone,
for working overtime so late.

271
00:19:06,350 --> 00:19:08,220
CEO Jeon, let me take that for you.

272
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:12,760
I figured you hadn't eaten dinner.

273
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:15,230
I am not interrupting, am I?

274
00:19:15,490 --> 00:19:18,100
Not at all.
You must be busy too, CEO Jeon,

275
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,660
yet you came all this way
to cheer us on.

276
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:20,860
We are so touched.

277
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:23,470
It smells amazing.

278
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:26,840
It is fried chicken.

279
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:29,140
We were just wondering
what snack to order.

280
00:19:29,610 --> 00:19:30,610
Thank you, CEO Jeon.

281
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:32,640
Looks delicious, CEO Jeon.

282
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:40,980
CEO Jeon.

283
00:19:43,890 --> 00:19:44,920
Please sit over here.

284
00:19:46,190 --> 00:19:48,490
I was just going
to drop it off and go.

285
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:52,060
May I sit and join you?

286
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:54,030
Manager Kang,
I mean, Assistant Kang.

287
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:57,600
Of course, CEO Jeon. Have a seat.

288
00:19:57,870 --> 00:19:58,870
Thank you.

289
00:20:01,940 --> 00:20:03,070
Let us dig in, everyone.

290
00:20:04,410 --> 00:20:07,040
Fried chicken is always best
when it is hot.

291
00:20:19,090 --> 00:20:20,820
Why aren't you eating, Da Mi?

292
00:20:22,430 --> 00:20:24,190
I am fine, thank you.

293
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:28,470
CEO Jeon bought this for us.
Have a piece.

294
00:20:36,070 --> 00:20:38,010
Excuse me.
I need to use the restroom.

295
00:20:45,920 --> 00:20:47,050
Excuse me for a moment.

296
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:58,330
Come to think of it,
we do not have cola.

297
00:20:58,430 --> 00:21:00,360
I'll go buy some right away.
Go ahead without me.

298
00:21:24,220 --> 00:21:25,860
Do you have an allergy to chicken?

299
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,690
Or do you have
bad memories associated with it?

300
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,830
Are you refusing
because CEO Jeon bought it?

301
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:36,070
Head Designer Cha, why aren't you
eating with them?

302
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,370
- Did you come out looking for me?
- What about you, Kang Da Mi?

303
00:21:39,770 --> 00:21:41,670
You said you'd go to the restroom.
Why are you here?

304
00:21:44,780 --> 00:21:46,380
You don't have to answer
if you don't want to.

305
00:21:48,710 --> 00:21:49,710
Actually,

306
00:21:51,750 --> 00:21:53,180
the last thing...

307
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:56,090
my birth mother bought me
was fried chicken.

308
00:21:58,990 --> 00:22:00,690
Not knowing
it would be the last time,

309
00:22:00,760 --> 00:22:02,330
I really enjoyed eating it.

310
00:22:03,730 --> 00:22:05,930
But I had no idea that day...

311
00:22:05,930 --> 00:22:10,030
my birth mother would abandon me
right there.

312
00:22:11,440 --> 00:22:12,800
Ever since that day,

313
00:22:13,370 --> 00:22:16,040
whenever I see fried chicken,
it brings back memories.

314
00:22:17,140 --> 00:22:18,310
That is why I don't eat it.

315
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:21,850
That must have hurt deeply.

316
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:29,150
It is just food,
so it is strange, right?

317
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:34,090
So much time has passed,
and I am living well now.

318
00:22:36,590 --> 00:22:38,100
I don't think it is strange at all.

319
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:41,330
No matter how much time passes,

320
00:22:42,070 --> 00:22:45,270
doesn't everyone have memories
they can never forget?

321
00:22:50,170 --> 00:22:53,340
CEO Jeon bought it,
so it was hard to refuse,

322
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:56,980
and I didn't want to explain
my personal history either.

323
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:59,420
So I just stepped out.

324
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:01,950
Kang Da Mi.

325
00:23:04,220 --> 00:23:07,620
When you truly dislike something
or really don't want to do it,

326
00:23:08,530 --> 00:23:10,360
it is okay to just say
you don't like it.

327
00:23:11,330 --> 00:23:12,430
I mean that...

328
00:23:12,430 --> 00:23:14,260
you don't have to try so hard
to accommodate others.

329
00:23:14,630 --> 00:23:15,630
No matter who it is.

330
00:23:16,230 --> 00:23:17,230
Understood?

331
00:23:28,510 --> 00:23:29,510
Oh my.

332
00:23:31,620 --> 00:23:33,550
See? Aren't you glad
I insisted on taking photos?

333
00:23:35,320 --> 00:23:38,460
Look at this last picture.
It turned out great, didn't it?

334
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:40,760
It really did.

335
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:45,460
I haven't seen Mom smile like this
in decades.

336
00:23:46,260 --> 00:23:47,500
At first, Mother said no...

337
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,030
and only posed because we insisted.

338
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,840
But I stood beside her and kept
saying, "Mother, smile! Smile!"

339
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:54,270
I kept at it until we got this shot.

340
00:23:54,300 --> 00:23:55,570
You have to give me credit
for this, right?

341
00:23:55,640 --> 00:23:56,640
Of course.

342
00:24:00,210 --> 00:24:02,150
Are you crying, honey?

343
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:05,720
Who says I am crying?

344
00:24:08,490 --> 00:24:11,350
Oh my. I haven't sent the photo
to Mother yet.

345
00:24:11,450 --> 00:24:12,490
I should send it to her.

346
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:15,690
Yes, do that. Send it right away.

347
00:24:16,030 --> 00:24:17,660
- You have your phone, right?
- Yes.

348
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:20,530
Look at Mom. Isn't she adorable?

349
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,930
Hey, isn't my mom pretty?

350
00:24:23,470 --> 00:24:25,200
- It turned out well.
- Totally.

351
00:24:31,580 --> 00:24:34,710
What is this?
Who is texting at this hour?

352
00:24:36,610 --> 00:24:37,610
Mother,

353
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,680
it is your daughter-in-law,
Ji Young.

354
00:24:39,950 --> 00:24:42,790
The family photo turned out
so nicely, so I am sending it.

355
00:24:58,870 --> 00:24:59,870
Mother.

356
00:25:00,540 --> 00:25:01,640
Yes, dear?

357
00:25:03,170 --> 00:25:04,470
Excuse me a second,
let me have that.

358
00:25:05,210 --> 00:25:06,840
Dear, this is...

359
00:25:07,780 --> 00:25:09,410
Not the phone, my book.

360
00:25:09,950 --> 00:25:12,750
You are sitting on my book
right now.

361
00:25:15,020 --> 00:25:17,990
You mean this? Here you go.

362
00:25:20,890 --> 00:25:22,460
I will be back in a little bit.

363
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:25,930
Where are you going
this late in the evening?

364
00:25:28,830 --> 00:25:30,130
All right.

365
00:25:30,730 --> 00:25:31,770
Go ahead.

366
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:36,470
Just make sure you come back home.

367
00:25:47,750 --> 00:25:48,890
It is me, Mother.

368
00:25:55,830 --> 00:25:57,090
Mother, did you take your medicine?

369
00:25:57,560 --> 00:25:59,500
Yes, I was just about to.

370
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,330
Take it with this tea.

371
00:26:04,300 --> 00:26:05,570
I let it cool down a bit...

372
00:26:06,070 --> 00:26:07,100
so it's not too hot.

373
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:08,840
All right.

374
00:26:26,190 --> 00:26:30,030
It was a good thing
I got my supplements in advance.

375
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:44,540
I'll be heading out now, CEO Jeon.

376
00:26:47,140 --> 00:26:48,140
Manager Kang.

377
00:26:48,680 --> 00:26:49,680
Yes?

378
00:26:50,210 --> 00:26:51,410
About the chicken earlier,

379
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:53,920
by any chance,

380
00:26:54,150 --> 00:26:56,550
did you refuse to eat it on purpose
because I bought it?

381
00:26:57,790 --> 00:27:00,490
- No, CEO Jeon.
- You did not?

382
00:27:01,190 --> 00:27:02,230
You are saying I misunderstood?

383
00:27:03,630 --> 00:27:04,630
Yes.

384
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:09,670
Now that I look at you,
you are not very honest, are you?

385
00:27:10,630 --> 00:27:12,000
Because of what happened
at the store,

386
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:14,670
I know very well
you hold a grudge against me.

387
00:27:18,740 --> 00:27:20,310
Mom?

388
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:26,380
Mom?

389
00:27:49,110 --> 00:27:51,070
(Mission: Mompossible)

390
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:10,030
Please make sure Ms. Jo
gets some rest from now on.

391
00:28:10,260 --> 00:28:11,800
She must not overexert herself
under any circumstances.

392
00:28:11,860 --> 00:28:14,430
Could Dr. Ju have feelings
for my sister?

393
00:28:14,700 --> 00:28:16,170
I asked Kang Da Mi,

394
00:28:16,230 --> 00:28:18,100
and she said she does not
really like chicken.

395
00:28:18,200 --> 00:28:21,240
The last thing her birth mother
bought her was fried chicken.

396
00:28:21,300 --> 00:28:23,210
Then that woman earlier
was not her birth mother...

397
00:28:23,310 --> 00:28:24,670
but her adoptive mother.

398
00:28:25,710 --> 00:28:27,710
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
